Tricky Interview Question of DevOps:

90% engineers misunderstand this Kubernetes concept ⚠️

What is Requests and limits in kubernetes? 

Answer:

In simple words:

💡 Requests = Minimum guaranteed resources
💡 Limits = Maximum allowed resources


🧠 Think like this:

• Request → “I NEED at least this much to run”
• Limit → “I CANNOT go beyond this”
🚨 What actually happens?


If the CPU exceeds the limit →

👉 Kubernetes throttles your container
👉 App becomes slow 🐢

If Memory exceeds limit →

👉 Container is KILLED(OOMKilled) 💀
👉 Pod restarts


🔥 Real Example:

inside a container YAML file: 

resources:
  requests:
    cpu: "200m"
    memory: "256Mi"
  limits:
    cpu: "500m"
    memory: "512Mi"

✔ Guaranteed: 200m CPU, 256Mi RAM
❌ Cannot exceed: 500m CPU, 512Mi RAM
